From df8b6d78b7b42655bb9446ab881a16c8d66a0c2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:47:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] test(test-backend-ops): add Qwen MTP and QSA verify flash
 attention cases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The FA eval loop only uses gqa 12 for head size 128, so the 256/256
gqa 12 F16 shape of the Qwen MTP layer had no dense case. Add dense eval
cases at kv 1024 for one row (split-KV path) and four rows (row-chunk
path), with and without sinks. Add a four-row QSA verify case with the
n_kv_max 2048 budget.

Add perf cases for the same dense shape at kv 8192, 32768 and 131072,
for one and four rows, to measure the batch-1 decode kernel at depth.

These cases cover the decode kernel change from upstream llama.cpp
PR #27478. With -b CPU, the reference path runs the same one_chunk
function, so these cases cannot catch a bug in the blocked loop. The
checks for that are a dump comparison against the base build and a KLD
run.

